## Environment variables

### `backend/.env`

| Variable | Example | Description |
|---|---|---|
| `PORT` | `5000` | API port |
| `NODE_ENV` | `development` | `development` or `production` |
| `MONGODB_URI` | `mongodb://127.0.0.1:27017/10xdevss` | MongoDB connection string (**required**) |
| `ALLOWED_ORIGINS` | `http://localhost:5173` | Comma-separated list of frontend origins allowed by CORS |
| `JWT_ACCESS_SECRET` | long random string | Signs access tokens |
| `JWT_REFRESH_SECRET` | different long random string | Signs refresh tokens |
| `JWT_ACCESS_EXPIRES_IN` | `15m` | Access token lifetime |
| `JWT_REFRESH_EXPIRES_IN` | `7d` | Refresh token lifetime |
| `RESEND_API_KEY` | `re_xxx` | Resend API key |
| `RESEND_FROM_EMAIL` | `onboarding@resend.dev` | Sender address (use a verified domain in production) |
| `IMAGEKIT_PUBLIC_KEY` | | ImageKit public key |
| `IMAGEKIT_PRIVATE_KEY` | | ImageKit private key (**never expose to the frontend**) |
| `IMAGEKIT_AUTH_TTL_SECONDS` | `600` | Lifetime of each upload signature |

Generate strong secrets with:

```bash
node -e "console.log(require('crypto').randomBytes(64).toString('hex'))"
```

### `10xdevss/.env`

| Variable | Example | Description |
|---|---|---|
| `VITE_BACKEND_URL` | `http://localhost:5000` | Backend base URL |
| `VITE_IMAGEKIT_PUBLIC_KEY` | | ImageKit public key |
| `VITE_IMAGEKIT_URL_ENDPOINT` | `https://ik.imagekit.io/your_id` | ImageKit URL endpoint |
| `VITE_IMAGEKIT_AUTH_ENDPOINT` | `http://localhost:5000/api/imagekit/auth` | Backend endpoint that signs uploads |

> `.env` files are git-ignored. Only the `.env.example` files are committed. Never commit real keys.

